{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1150275-what-is-modus-operandi-of-the-iteration-x-soft-scientists","id":1150275,"title":"What is modus operandi of the Iteration X soft scientists?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-16T23:30:33-07:00","id":1150275,"title":"What is modus operandi of the Iteration X soft scientists?","content":"According to It-X Convention Book, the Statisticians contain huge number of psychologists, sociologists, social engineers and futurologists and other &quot;soft&quot; scientists . What is their job in the Machine Convention? What would be their assignment, duty and responsibility? Have you any ideas&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T08:14:51-07:00","id":1150358,"title":"","content":"Prediction. Social Engineering.<br /> <br /> Iteration X does not hold to the belief that it's better to try and fail than not try at all. They do believe however that victory is just a matter of making the right decisions. To make the right decisions, you need information to base it upon.<br /> <br /> Social Engineering, because their internal culture is vastly different to the point of causing discomfort in new recruits because of culture shock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T12:15:49-07:00","id":1150413,"title":"","content":"Essentially, Iteration X wants to know how people 'tick' so they can make them as reliable as a clock. There will be a lot of data to crunch with Entropy and a lot trying to convince people to be regular. Think of trying to shift pre-Industrial societies with time based on natural happenings to factory time and you see how busy ItX soft scientists are. I also imagine quite a few are working to reduce people's fears of machines that some sci-fi movies promote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T13:58:36-07:00","id":1150460,"title":"","content":"The Convention is built around the idea that the universe and everything in it is one big machine and therefore can be perfected with the right engineering. With the Statisticians, they take the &quot;software&quot; approach, using a massive amount of math and utilitarian psychology. They investigate existing problems and try to foreseer potential future ones and then work out ways to fix them or head them off. And a good deal of this does involve social engineering for their desired public ethos and mindsets (something that probably involves cooperation with the NWO and/or Syndicate.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T18:15:46-07:00","id":1150512,"title":"","content":"I also imagine many of them work heavily with computer programmers - if they aren't programmers themselves - in order to develop and improve Artificial Intelligence. Both to embed into larger systems that can control things on an industrial or even societal level (in a world of greater technological integration, you need some kind of intelligence running the show at speeds humans can't), and on the individual level (robots need AI to function, if you want them to react dynamically in the world).<br /> <br /> All that requires an understanding of psychology (in order to properly replicate it in neural networks, as well as to make sure it has functioning Ethical codes that prevent it from going full Skynet on you). So while some Iterators are working to make better machines, others are working on how to make them smarter...while at the same time keeping them compliant and amenable to the needs of Humanity. I suspect others in this field work heavily with the Biomechanics to integrate humanity's native wetware and the cybernetic implants the Convention loves to play with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T18:34:53-07:00","id":1150515,"title":"","content":"They're cyberneticians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T05:19:45-07:00","id":1150608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1150275-what-is-modus-operandi-of-the-iteration-x-soft-scientists#post1150275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to It-X Convention Book, the Statisticians contain huge number of psychologists, sociologists, social engineers and futurologists and other &quot;soft&quot; scientists . What is their job in the Machine Convention? What would be their assignment, duty and responsibility? Have you any ideas&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>One of their main jobs is directing other True Mages of the Iteration-X. Another key job they would be doing within their Convention would be directing the Extraordinary Citizens of the Iteration-X.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T08:35:11-07:00","id":1150654,"title":"","content":"Or there primary job is coordinate the intrinsic systems of the Convention to maximize efficiency in accordance with the Time Line and the goals of Iteration X. They are efficiency experts trying to create the ultimate assembly line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T13:22:33-07:00","id":1150752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1150275-what-is-modus-operandi-of-the-iteration-x-soft-scientists?p=1150654#post1150654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or there primary job is coordinate the intrinsic systems of the Convention to maximize efficiency in accordance with the Time Line and the goals of Iteration X. They are efficiency experts trying to create the ultimate assembly line.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have thought that is explicitly purpose of the TM Managers...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T18:53:53-07:00","id":1150868,"title":"","content":"Also, from the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Statisticians\" target=\"_blank\">White Wolf Wiki</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The three main goals of the Methodology are gathering data and compiling databases, modeling and forecasting from that data, and then putting that information to use. If the data isn't used or explored in some way it's useless... dead data.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>So, for all of the soft scientists, their role is gathering information in their field of study and finding ways to apply it in the field. One example would be <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Environmental_psychology\" target=\"_blank\">architectural psychology</a>, and figuring out how to use its principles to design work places and living spaces that encourage and reinforce the sort of mindsets and world views the Convention wants people to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 10-18-2017, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}